  "body": "**What:** PR #999 (#862) adds the guard `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes`. Every posted NC golden whose stem has a `.cl` golden must verify clean, carry a \"refused program, posted for syntax conformance\" first line, or be named in `UNJUDGED` with a reason. Six goldens sit in `UNJUDGED`: the two slot goldens, `trochoid_slot_small`, `trace_plate_with_hole`, `arc_planes` and `plasma_plate_with_holes`. No test checks their posted programs against the gate the user's post would run. `plasma_plate_with_holes` isn't run through the plasma gate in this suite at all.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is the risk #862 closed for two fixtures. A posted golden for a program the gate would refuse reads as \"this output is right\". Being in `UNJUDGED` means \"not checked\", not \"checked clean\".\n\n**Done means:** each `UNJUDGED` entry is judged by the gate its program really meets (depth laws where they apply; the plasma gate for the plasma plate) and removed from the list, or kept with a stated reason why no gate applies; the list shrinks to only those; any golden whose program the gate refuses is fixed as in #862.\n\nDepends on PR #999 merging. Found by the #862 worker (SKULL).\n",
